  "question": {
    "text": "Let the area of the bounded region $\\left\\{(x, y): 0 \\leq 9 x \\leq y^2, y \\geq 3 x-6\\right\\}$ be A. Then 6 A is equal to ________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "15",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$0 \\leq 9 x \\leq y^2 \\& y \\geq 3 x-6$<br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/Da8qHrCALHOGwq_3pBACHXdtKT7b5kLf84a16lbmci8.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\begin{aligned} & A=\\text { Required Area }=\\left[\\int_0^1(-3 \\sqrt{x}) d x-\\int_0^1(3 x-6) d x\\right] \\\\ & A=-\\left.3\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right)\\right|_0 ^1-\\left.\\left(\\frac{3 x^2}{2}-6 x\\right)\\right|_0 ^1 \\\\ & A=-2[1-0]\\left[\\frac{3}{2}-6\\right] \\\\ & A=-2-\\frac{3}{2}+6=\\frac{5}{2} \\text { Sq. unit } \\\\ & \\therefore 6 A=6 \\times \\frac{5}{2}=15\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
